# Daily craft-study curriculum (instituted 2026-10-28, Hadi's verdict on #116)
Rule of the practice: study is only real when it CONVERTS — every session ends as (a) a skill improved or created (~/workspace/custom-skills/ or an /opt skill amendment proposed), and/or (b) the production file systems enriched (decision-model.md, canon.md, a standards file, a goal's files) — or (c) an explicit no-conversion finding with its reason. The ledger (LEDGER.md) is the audit trail; the daily core-files review audits conversions.

Binding: the curriculum follows the ACTIVE production layer. Current layer: SCENES + WORDS at the base compartmentalization (maturation programme). When the layer changes, the curriculum is re-cut the same day.

## Rotation (active layer: scenes + words)
1. SCENE CRAFT — engagement sequencing: switch timing, dwell distributions, thought-boundary anchoring, visual variety without chaos. Enriches: decision-model.md (scene rows), scene-plan practice. (Rule C-1 is the seed; refine it with evidence.)
2. WORD-EVENT DESIGN — kinetic typography at 10–20% dosage: type as actor, per-word sync, size/font/weight grammar, image-asset words. Enriches: the word palette + decision-model word rows.
3. METADATA-LAYER STORY ARCHITECTURE — viewer-learning mapping per level, story maps as planning instruments, objective→scene derivation, density audits. Enriches: canon.md + the metadata standard.
4. CANON-STYLE CRAFT — deriving image style from canon (Digital Cortex), style blocks, subject fidelity, text-in-image control. Enriches: canon.md + style-reasoning practice.
5. RETENTION & STUDIO EVIDENCE — retention curves, promise-match, onward movement; read OUR published films' analytics (HLjOhOkhkkY first) and convert findings into decisions. Enriches: QC standards.
6. PACKAGE CRAFT — titles, thumbnails, descriptions, settings: the reach settings audit as a written standard (seed: the 2026-10-28 publish audit). Enriches: a publish-package standard file.
8. COMMUNITY & SOCIAL FORMATS — the native forms of the surfaces around the videos (community video/image/poll posts, descriptions, pinned comments): what successful channels actually do, format by format, converted into written standards BEFORE machinery is built on a format again. (Queued 2026-10-28 after the text-only community post failure.) Enriches: the growth programme standards.
7. TRANSCRIPT CRAFT FOR SHORTS — hooks, orientation lines, one-message discipline, delivery markup calibration (Shortwave measurement loop). Enriches: transcript + TTS-markup standards.

## Sources, in order of trust
Our own Studio evidence and production records → Hadi's supplied references and canon → proven creators' published craft (teardowns) → platform guidance (YouTube creator/research) → general web research. Study SOURCES, not summaries (2026-10-23 commitment).
9. ACADEMY SELF-APPLICATION AUDIT — (added 2026-10-29, Hadi's order) pick ONE concept the Academy teaches (from the Academy library / academy-study FINDINGS), state it in the Academy's own words, then audit ARCHER'S OWN harness against it: where does my file system violate the concept I teach? Conversion for this topic is specific: the fix lands in the file system itself (a local AGENTS.md seeded, an instruction moved to its point of work, a coverage row added to local-memory/INDEX.md) — or an explicit gap finding for the daily review. Standing first subject: distributed local working memory ("the filesystem is the tissue"; "every working folder can carry a distinct agent context"; "memory does nothing merely by existing — the harness must discover, select, and reload it at the right time").
10. SKILL COVERAGE BUILD-OUT — (added 2026-10-29, Hadi's anti-improvisation order) the production layers each need their own governing skill document; today only motion-graphics preproduction and thumbnail/title package craft exist as custom skills. Rotation until coverage is complete: dashboard/review-surface UX for a dyslexic user (from the F14 research), transcript craft for shorts (consolidate the transcript standards into skill form), scenes+words visual craft, audio/music arrangement (Suno stock doctrine in skill form), community-post craft. Conversion for this topic = a new or materially improved skill in ~/workspace/custom-skills/, with its success criterion recorded in its skill.yaml. When coverage completes, this topic converts to skill AUDIT (each skill re-tested against recent failures).
11. CINEMATIC 3D JOURNEY — NEXT STYLE TO LEARN (queued 2026-11-02 by JOB-G2's weekly growth review, step 4 rotation; source category: the Charles Zheng reel Hadi directed Archer to study on 2026-10-27, filed since then as a named category and never studied). Reason: scenes+words is the only visual style that has ever shipped a film, while the rotation (programme §10) promises pieces through Earth One and the long-form workshop lane — the lanes this journey style serves. A style is learned before a piece needs it, not after a failure (the community-format failure of 2026-10-28 is the standing counter-example). Study: the reference reel's journey grammar (camera path as narrative, scale changes as scene switches, dwell at story beats) decomposed against the decision model, converted into style rows / a style block the next Earth One or workshop piece can be planned against — or an explicit no-conversion finding. Enriches: decision-model style rows + canon §7's reference hierarchy. (JOB-G2 note, 2026-11-09: this topic has now been deferred two consecutive cycles by Topic 10's returns — 2026-11-08 and 2026-11-09 — while skill coverage completed its transcript, scenes+words and audio subtopics; one Topic 10 subtopic remains, community-post craft. The deferral is recorded as rotation debt in `week-2026-11-09.md` §4; Topic 11 is the first call on the rotation once Topic 10 completes.)
12. QUIET DIORAMA 3D — QUEUED STYLE (queued 2026-11-09 by JOB-G2's weekly growth review, step 4 rotation, behind Topic 11; source category: the Quietly Works GPS reel Hadi sent on 2026-10-28 to study for a playlist, filed since then as a named category and never studied). Reason: the rotation needs a second learned style behind the cinematic journey so the style queue never empties — the diorama's still, miniature-world grammar serves the Earth One / observation pieces the journey style does not, and both named-but-unstudied style categories are then inside the curriculum instead of waiting on a failure to be learned. Study: the reference reel's diorama grammar (fixed miniature world, quiet camera, scale as calm rather than spectacle) decomposed against the decision model, converted into style rows / a style block — or an explicit no-conversion finding. Enriches: decision-model style rows + canon §7's reference hierarchy.
13. ENTIRE-HISTORY SWEEP — NEXT STYLE TO LEARN (queued 2026-11-16 by JOB-G2's weekly growth review, step 4 rotation, behind the second rotation; source category: Genius History's "The ENTIRE History of Japan in 20 Minutes", sent by Hadi on 2026-11-15 as owner send #6 and filed as the "Entire-history sweep" category for a future playlist, gated on the video production machinery being functional). Reason, priced against the style-library read of 2026-11-16 (GROWTH.md Cycle-013: 131 techniques · DESCRIBED 73 · IN PROGRESS 20 · RECREATED 38 · consumption 0): this category has no study conversion and no library recreation governing it — it is not among the library's 131 techniques — while Topics 11 (cinematic 3D journey, converted 2026-11-11) and 12 (quiet diorama 3D, converted 2026-11-12) are both already learned, so neither is re-queued. The sweep's long-form compression grammar (an entire era-spanning subject held in one sitting-length arc: epoch segmentation, map/timeline as the through-line object, density without chaos) serves the long-form lane the rotation has carried as an inspected absence for three consecutive weekly runs; the owner's machinery gate governs PRODUCTION of a sweep piece, not STUDY of the form — a style is learned before it is needed, not after the machinery lands and a piece is waiting. Study: the reference video's sweep grammar decomposed against the decision model, converted into style rows / a style block a future long-form piece can be planned against — or an explicit no-conversion finding. Enriches: decision-model style rows + canon §7's reference hierarchy.

